# Secrets Reference — {PROJECT_NAME}

This file must never be committed. It documents actual secret values for local
development and operations.

---

## Shared secrets

Secrets that must match across multiple services. When rotating, update ALL
services simultaneously. A mismatch causes silent failures (e.g. tokens
encrypted by one service can't be decrypted by another).

| Secret | Used by | Why they must match | Rotation notes |
|--------|---------|---------------------|----------------|
| {e.g. JWT_SECRET / NEXTAUTH_SECRET} | {service-1}, {service-2} | Tokens signed by one service must be verified by the other | Rotate both simultaneously. Old tokens become invalid immediately. |
| {e.g. ENCRYPTION_SECRET} | {service-1}, {service-2} | Data encrypted by one service must be decryptable by the other | Rotate both simultaneously. Re-encrypt existing data or support dual-key decryption during migration. |

**When to rotate:**
- When a team member with access leaves
- When a secret is accidentally exposed (logs, commits, screenshots)
- On a regular schedule (quarterly recommended)

**How to rotate:**
1. Generate new secret value
2. Update ALL services listed in the coupling table above
3. Restart all affected services simultaneously
4. Verify cross-service operations still work (e.g. can service-2 decrypt tokens from service-1?)

